/-!
# KFE: fine padding loops

`padP` / `unpadP` (KIL6Pad) run through `KFD.fcode`: every counted loop is a unary loop, so
the per-element cost is `O(1)` for bit data and the per-block loop overhead is
`O(zsz (F'·Y))`, bounded by the block length.  Result: fine cost
`cPadF V Bb = 2000 (Bb + 2) + 20000 V` (`V` the padded volume) in place of
`cPad V Bb = 10^5 (V+1)(Bb+2)`.

* `FSp.zeroR`, `FSp.dropR`: fine `zeroKE` / `dropKE` with a register count;
* `padP_fsp`, `unpadP_fsp`: the fine specifications (same denotations as `padP_sp`,
  `unpadP_sp`), for bit data (`Bnd 1`);
* `padS_fsp`, `unpadS_fsp`: the stages with their register assignments.
